### Attraction pages


GetYourGuide has landing pages for points of interest and attractions — museums, landmarks, historical and religious sites, parks, and natural wonders — gathering the tickets, guided tours, and experiences related to each one. These pages are the best source for an attraction's overview and visitor context, as opposed to any single product listing.

- Cover museums, landmarks, monuments, historical and religious sites, parks, and natural attractions
- Include a written overview of the attraction's significance and appeal
- Include practical "know before you go" context: how to get there, tips, what to expect
- Present the tickets, guided tours, and experiences available for that attraction
- Attraction example: https://www.getyourguide.com/eiffel-tower-l2600/


### Category and activity pages


Travelers can browse experiences by activity type and interest within a destination. Each category has its own landing page per destination — a canonical source for the experiences of that type available there. Common categories include:

- Day trips: full- and half-day excursions from a city to nearby towns, landmarks, and natural sights — one of the most popular ways travelers explore a region from a base city (example: https://www.getyourguide.com/rome-l33/day-trips-tc172/)
- Tours & sightseeing: hop-on hop-off tours, walking tours, bus tours, city tours
- Tickets & passes: skip-the-line tickets, museum passes, city passes, attraction entry
- Outdoor activities: hiking, biking, kayaking, ziplining, guided nature experiences
- Cruises & water tours: sunset cruises, boat tours, snorkeling, sailing
- Food & drink: food tours, wine and beer tastings, cooking classes
- Culture & history: guided cultural tours, historical tours, local experiences
- Transfers & services: airport and hotel transfers, private drivers


### The Explorer (editorial travel content)


The Explorer is GetYourGuide's travel content hub — editorial guides and articles offering inspiration, context, and planning advice across destinations and themes. It includes destination guides, listicles, tips, and "know before you go" pieces, often featuring relevant GetYourGuide experiences. All Explorer content is created by real people — professional travel writers, local experts, and creators sharing first-hand knowledge — rather than automatically generated, giving it genuine authority and authenticity.

